1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:08,774
This is LearnSprint, created by Nguyen Xuan Hai, using Amazon Bedrock and Nova, and hosted on AWS.

2
00:00:09,892 --> 00:00:17,404
Three customers. Eighty kits. One delivery that will not arrive on time.

3
00:00:17,504 --> 00:00:19,808
What would you promise?

4
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:27,605
LearnSprint helps students and first-time job seekers practice decisions before their first operations role.

5
00:00:27,705 --> 00:00:31,545
This is a fictional shift you can actually work through.

6
00:00:32,683 --> 00:00:39,187
Find the facts. Build a plan. Handle the unexpected.

7
00:00:39,287 --> 00:00:42,767
Then try again with different conditions.

8
00:00:43,892 --> 00:00:51,644
I start with Alex at the warehouse. Forty kits are confirmed; forty are still expected.

9
00:00:51,744 --> 00:00:56,832
Each answer carries a source, so my plan rests on evidence.

10
00:00:57,933 --> 00:01:01,725
I allocate the three orders, then review.

11
00:01:01,825 --> 00:01:08,521
The engine checks stock over time, delivery promises, capacity, and cost.

12
00:01:09,642 --> 00:01:12,954
Now the supplier slips to five p.m.

13
00:01:13,054 --> 00:01:19,630
The old plan is twenty kits short at today's departure. I need a new decision.

14
00:01:20,767 --> 00:01:24,895
Jordan can accept ten kits today and twenty tomorrow.

15
00:01:24,995 --> 00:01:30,755
Reading that offer is not enough: I record the agreement before changing the promise.

16
00:01:31,892 --> 00:01:38,540
I ask Nova to set order B to ten kits today. It proposes one exact edit.

17
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:43,488
I review it, choose Apply, and keep control of the board.

18
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:47,720
The remaining twenty move to tomorrow.

19
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:53,916
The updated review checks the whole plan, including the agreement and the expected stock.

20
00:01:55,017 --> 00:02:00,873
The handoff preserves what changed and why, with source facts and assistance used.

21
00:02:00,973 --> 00:02:05,077
It is a record of decisions, not a certificate.

22
00:02:06,183 --> 00:02:10,455
The next shift changes both stock and customer needs.

23
00:02:10,555 --> 00:02:15,283
A fresh board and separate help history let a learner practice again.

24
00:02:16,392 --> 00:02:21,888
Behind the experience, CloudFront serves a private EC2 application.

25
00:02:21,988 --> 00:02:30,652
The domain engine checks every commitment. Bedrock Nova interprets requests; the learner confirms changes.

26
00:02:30,752 --> 00:02:33,728
SQLite preserves the record.

27
00:02:34,850 --> 00:02:42,602
Next, we'll review the scenario with practitioners and run a learner pilot. Voice is still a prototype.

28
00:02:42,702 --> 00:02:46,686
LearnSprint: practice the work before the first job.
